      "writtenOn": "2020-02-26T01:04:02Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I know this is not added as part of this change, but I am trying to remember why this function toggles the state of the button? It looks like it is expecting to return one particular state of a button when simulated_button_pressed() is called for the first time and then returns flipped state when simulate_button_pressed() is called the second time. Can\u0027t this be handled by simulate_button() and simulate_button_release()?\n\ni.e.\nsimulate_button --\u003e Updates sim_button_state to be pressed for given button\nsimulate_button_release --\u003e Updates sim_button_state to be released for given button\n\nsimulated_button_pressed --\u003e Returns current state as per sim_button_state for given button.",
      "range": {
